<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        BUG-13 (ClickUp 869f03wub): the stock Odoo "Odoo Information" page
        (route /website/info, core module `website`) is publicly reachable
        by design and dumps the company name as "<db name> — Information
        about the <db name> instance of Odoo" plus the full list of
        installed apps. On some instances the database is named in a way that identifies the
        customer or vendor, so the page can literally advertise that
        information and leaks the installed-app list to anyone who guesses
        the URL.

        The core template itself says how to turn it off ("To hide this
        page, uncheck it from the Customize tab in edit mode" - see
        addons/website/views/website_templates.xml, template
        website.show_website_info). We do that from data so it ships
        disabled by default instead of relying on someone remembering to
        toggle it in the editor.

        We only deactivate website.show_website_info, the inherited view
        that renders the actual company-name/app-list/version content.
        That empties #wrap entirely (verified locally: renders as
        `<div id="wrap" class="o_website_info"></div>`, no company name,
        no app list, no version string, no "demo" wording anywhere in the
        response body) and makes controller sitemap_website_info()
        exclude /website/info from /sitemap.xml, satisfying the ticket's
        "shows production-appropriate information" acceptance criterion.

        We deliberately do NOT also deactivate the base website.website_info
        view. Tried that first locally: with both views inactive, Odoo's
        `_get_view_id` raises `ValueError: View 'website.website_info' in
        website 1 not found`, which the frontend turns into a bare
        Odoo/werkzeug 500 error page instead of a 404 - worse for a
        production site than a normal blank page (spurious entries in
        error monitoring/logs for a URL that isn't even linked anywhere).
        Leaving website.website_info active keeps /website/info returning
        a normal 200 page using the site's own header/footer/theme, just
        with nothing inside it - no information disclosure, no error noise.
    -->
    <record id="website.show_website_info" model="ir.ui.view">
        <field name="active">False</field>
    </record>
</odoo>
